course: dictionary
lesson: 15715
title: Toxicity: poison and unkind words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Toxicity is a noun. It describes how poisonous or harmful something is. Scientists, doctors and safety labels use it about chemicals, plants and medicines. «The label warned about the high toxicity of the cleaning liquid.» The label is telling you the liquid can do a lot of harm, so you must keep it away from children.
explain: People also use toxicity in an informal way. It can mean nasty, unkind or harmful behaviour between people, especially online. «The teacher stopped the online toxicity in the class chat before anyone got hurt.» The word is about unkind messages, not poison.
explain: Look at the clues around the word to decide which meaning fits. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a substance, or about how people treat each other? If the sentence talks about a label, a doctor or a plant, it means poison. If it talks about friends, messages or comments, it means unkind behaviour.
fact: Toxicity means how poisonous or harmful something is.
fact: «Toxicity» can also mean nasty, unkind or harmful behaviour between people, especially online.
fact: High toxicity means something can do a lot of harm. Low toxicity means it can do much less harm.
fact: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «The toxicity of the plant» means how poisonous the plant is.
fact: Toxicity is a noun, so it can also appear as the plural «toxicities».
exercise: «The label on the bottle warned about the high toxicity of the liquid.» What does toxicity mean here? | How long the liquid lasts | *How poisonous or harmful something is | How heavy the bottle is | How bright the colour is
exercise: Ella says, «The online toxicity in my group chat made me feel awful.» What does toxicity mean in this sentence? | *Nasty, unkind or harmful behaviour between people | A slow internet connection | Fast and friendly messages | Clear, bright pictures
exercise: «The scientists measured the toxicity of the plant.» Find and copy the word that means poisonous or harmful. | plant | *toxicity | scientists | measured
test: «Tom said the toxicity of the rumours was hurting his friends.» What does toxicity mean here? | Sleepiness | *Harmful, unkind behaviour | Tasty food | Loud music
test: «The label showed low toxicity, so the cleaner was safer to use at home.» What does low toxicity mean? | It smells really nice | It is very expensive | *It can do little harm | It is very strong and dangerous
exam: «A doctor checks the toxicity of a medicine before giving it.» Which word means nearly the same as toxicity in this sentence? | quietness | happiness | brightness | *harmfulness
